# Trivy waivers (ADR 009). One advisory id per line, each with a comment above it giving the
# reason, who accepted it and a review date. A waiver without a reason is not accepted in review.

# prom/alertmanager v0.34.1 (the newest release) is built with Go and modules that have these
# fixes upstream but no Alertmanager release yet. Exposure: only Prometheus reaches it, on the
# private Docker network (no published port); its only outbound connections are TLS to the
# hospital's mail server and Telegram. Accepted by the OPD Saathi team on 23 Oct 2026; each
# entry expires on 30 Nov 2026, when the scan fails again until Alertmanager is upgraded.
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-84445 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-11-30

# golang.org/x/net/html: denial of service through crafted HTML, in bin/alertmanager and
# bin/amtool. Fixed in x/net 0.62.0, which no Alertmanager release is built with yet: checked
# v0.34.1 (0.58.0), v0.34.2 (0.60.0), v0.35.0 and v0.35.1 (0.61.0) on 26 Nov 2026. Exposure as
# above: Alertmanager parses no HTML from outside; only Prometheus reaches it, on the private
# Docker network. Accepted by the owner on 26 Nov 2026; expires on 31 Dec 2026. Upgrading to
# v0.34.2 or later already removes the five entries above, and should be done before they
# expire on 30 Nov 2026.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-12-31

# nginx 1.30.6 in the web image's base, nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.30.6-alpine. Six
# advisories were published on 18 Nov 2026, fixed in nginx 1.30.7; the newest build of the
# base image is still 1.30.6 (checked 26 Nov 2026; the official nginx image has 1.30.8).
# Accepted by the owner on 26 Nov 2026; each entry expires on 10 Dec 2026, when the scan fails
# again until the base image is updated (Dependabot proposes the new digest).
# Not reachable in our configuration: the mail proxy module is not configured,
CVE-2026-113425 exp:2026-12-10
# HTTP/3 is not configured,
CVE-2026-121810 exp:2026-12-10
# and no proxied name uses a variable, and there is no SSI or mirror (the resolver bug).
CVE-2026-123634 exp:2026-12-10
# HTTP/2 (two critical bugs): switched off in infra/web/nginx.tls.conf until the fixed image.
CVE-2026-123007 exp:2026-12-10
CVE-2026-123633 exp:2026-12-10
# TLS 1.3: a crafted connection can hang one worker (denial of service, no data exposed).
# Applies to an HTTPS installation, which is inside the hospital network and has no fix but
# the new image; the plain-HTTP demo is not affected. TLS 1.3 stays on.
CVE-2026-118899 exp:2026-12-10
